# Scenario 1 — Auto Create Problem from Repeated Incidents

## Real-Time Scenario

In banking environments, users may report the same issue multiple times such as:

- ATM Server Down
- Payment Gateway Failure
- Login Authentication Failure

Instead of resolving the same incident repeatedly, the system should automatically create a Problem record to identify the root cause permanently.

---

# ITIL Concept

| Incident                           | Problem |

| Restores service quickly           | Finds root cause |
| Temporary fix                      | Permanent solution |

### Banking Example

| Incident          | Problem |

| ATM Down          | Root cause of ATM failures |
| Login Issue       | Authentication service issue |

---

# Goal

If 3 incidents are created with the same Short Description:

✅ Automatically create a Problem record.

---

# Tools & Concepts Used

- Business Rule
- GlideRecord
- Server-side scripting
- Incident table
- Problem table
- Record counting
- ITIL Incident & Problem Management

---

# Automation Flow

Incident Created
↓
Business Rule checks duplicate incidents
↓
If count >= 3
↓
Problem record created automatically

---

# Steps

## Step 1 — Create Business Rule

Navigate to:

System Definition → Business Rules

Click:

New

---

## Step 2 — Configure Business Rule

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Name | Auto Create Problem |
| Table | Incident |
| Active | True |
| Advanced | True |
| When | After |
| Insert | True |

---

# Why After Business Rule?

Because the Incident record must first be inserted into the database before checking duplicate counts.

---

# Step 3 — Add Script

```javascript
(function executeRule(current, previous) {

    // GlideRecord on Incident table
    var inc = new GlideRecord('incident');

    // Check same short description
    inc.addQuery('short_description', current.short_description);

    inc.query();

    // Count incidents
    var count = inc.getRowCount();

    // If 3 or more incidents exist
    if (count >= 3) {

        // Create Problem record
        var prob = new GlideRecord('problem');

        prob.initialize();

        prob.short_description =
            'Problem created for repeated incidents: ' +
            current.short_description;

        prob.description =
            'Multiple incidents detected with same issue.';

        var problemSysId = prob.insert();

        // Add work note to incident
        current.work_notes =
            'Problem record automatically created.';
    }

})(current, previous);
